-- Preservation for TAPL chapter 8's typed arithmetic expressions — Theorem
-- 8.3.3, proved in Thena's surface language.
--
-- IT BUILDS ON canonical.thena AND progress.thena AND MUST BE LOADED AFTER
-- BOTH. Thena has no module imports; it has a session, and globals declared by
-- one module are in scope for the next. This file needs Term, Ty, HasType from
-- the first and Step from the second.
--
-- With progress beside it this is type safety for the language: a well-typed
-- term never gets stuck, and evaluation never changes its type.
--
-- == How it is proved
--
-- INDUCTION ON THE STEP DERIVATION, not the typing one. Each of the ten rules
-- knows the shape of the term it acts on, so what each case needs is the typing
-- derivation taken apart at that shape — and that is the inner `case d of`, one
-- line, in the arm that needs it.
--
-- THE NINE INVERSION LEMMAS ARE GONE, and with them the trick this file used to
-- be worth reading for. A rule like E-PredZero has to produce `HasType zero U`
-- for the U the original derivation had, and all that is known about U is that
-- `pred t` had it — so U is `nat`. The old proof could not say that: it stated
-- a lemma `predAtNat`, *anything of type nat also has type U*, and let an
-- elimination motive do the rewriting it could not do directly. The split does
-- it: `tPred` is the only method that survives against `HasType (pred zero) U`,
-- and solving its equations IS `U = nat`, so the arm answers `tZero` and the
-- goal already reads `HasType zero nat`. The three `subst`s the `if` lemmas
-- needed go the same way — a constructor's own variables and the caller's are
-- the same variables once the split has unified them.
--
-- THE INDUCTION HYPOTHESIS IS THE RECURSIVE CALL. `preservation p p' sr bool d1`
-- in the `eIf` arm is not a call; elaboration ties it to the hypothesis the
-- method holds about `sr`. Nothing names a hypothesis binder, and the whole
-- statement is introduced at the top.

module Preservation where

preservation : forall (t : Term) (t' : Term) (s : Step t t') (U : Ty) (d : HasType t U) -> HasType t' U
preservation = \ t t' s U d -> induction s of
  { eIfTrue a2 a3 -> case d of { tIf c1 c2 c3 T d1 d2 d3 -> d2 }
  ; eIfFalse a2 a3 -> case d of { tIf c1 c2 c3 T d1 d2 d3 -> d3 }
  ; eIf p p' a2 a3 sr -> case d of
      { tIf c1 c2 c3 T d1 d2 d3 -> tIf p' c2 c3 T (preservation p p' sr bool d1) d2 d3 }
  ; eSucc p p' sr -> case d of
      { tSucc c1 dd -> tSucc p' (preservation p p' sr nat dd) }
  ; ePredZero -> case d of { tPred c1 dd -> tZero }
  ; ePredSucc v nv -> case d of
      { tPred c1 dd -> case dd of { tSucc c2 dd2 -> dd2 } }
  ; ePred p p' sr -> case d of
      { tPred c1 dd -> tPred p' (preservation p p' sr nat dd) }
  ; eIsZeroZero -> case d of { tIsZero c1 dd -> tTrue }
  ; eIsZeroSucc v nv -> case d of { tIsZero c1 dd -> tFalse }
  ; eIsZero p p' sr -> case d of
      { tIsZero c1 dd -> tIsZero p' (preservation p p' sr nat dd) } }
